  "instructions": [
    "Bake potatoes at 400\u00b0 for 1 hour until done. Cool.",
    "Cut in half lengthwise, scoop out pulp. Reserve skins for another use.",
    "Melt butter in pot over low heat.",
    "Add flour gradually, stir constantly until smooth and bubbly, about 1 minute.",
    "Gradually add milk, stirring.",
    "Stir in potato pulp, salt, pepper, 1c cheese, half the bacon, 1 Tbl green onion, and sour cream.",
    "Heat through \u2014 DO NOT BOIL.",
    "Stir in remaining cheese and green onion.",
    "Garnish with remaining bacon."
  ],
  "notes": "Reserved potato skins can be used for loaded potato skins another meal."
